# Antiferromagnetic NiO (AFM-II order) in its magnetic primitive cell.
#
# NiO is a rock-salt crystal (a = 4.17 A). Below the Neel temperature the Ni
# moments form ferromagnetic (111) sheets whose direction alternates from
# sheet to sheet. The magnetic primitive cell is rhombohedral and holds two
# Ni with opposite moments and two O. The moments (1.9 Bohr magnetons) lie in
# the (111) plane along the cubic [-1 -1 2] direction.
#
# The file lists every site explicitly (magnetic space group P1), as written
# by pymatgen's CifWriter(write_magmoms=True); the moment components are given
# along the crystal axes.
data_NiO
